  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Artboard Table",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Artboard Table\"**\n\nThe site is a grey work table with white sheets laid on it. Each section is one artboard: a borderless sheet with a barely-there 4px corner, no shadow, no outline. Type carries the page: Geist at weight 500 with tight negative tracking, set large and allowed to step in and out across lines like a sentence being spoken. Each sheet gets exactly one colour moment, a flat geometric shape in the brand's orange tones, usually oversized and cropped by the sheet's edge. Everything else is ink on white, or white on graphite in dark mode.\n\nThe world follows the visitor's system preference: a light table (#ececec under white) and a dark table (#0c0c0c under graphite #161616), with the orange tones re-tuned per mode. Density is calm: sheets are padded generously (56px at desktop), separated by 64px of bare canvas, held to a 1240px shell. Lists and data read as ruled text, hairline above each row, never as tiles or icon cards.\n\nThe mark is a lowercase \"d\" built from two flat shapes, a disc and a rounded bar, with its counter cut as a true transparent hole so it sits on any ground. The same construction, oversized, is the hero artboard's shape.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Grey canvas, borderless artboards (4px radius), depth by tone only",
      "Geist Variable at 500 for every heading, tracking between -0.015em and -0.05em",
      "One flat orange shape per artboard, cropped by the sheet edge",
      "Ink pill buttons, underlined text links, soft-fill fields",
      "Tick ruler as position indicator (page scroll in the hero, reel scroll under services)",
      "Light and dark by `prefers-color-scheme`, no toggle"
    ],
